{"url": "https://www.asgraduate.pitt.edu/student-life/resources-international-graduate-students", "final_url": "https://www.asgraduate.pitt.edu/student-life/resources-international-graduate-students", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-24", "text": "Resources for International Graduate Students | The Dietrich School of Arts & Sciences Graduate Studies | University of Pittsburgh\nSkip to main content\nThe Dietrich School of Arts & SciencesGraduate Studies\nToggle navigation\nSearch this site\nSearch\nSearch\nAbout\nOverview\nDoctoral Program Statistics\nDirectory\nGraduate Council\nAlumni\nOverview\nGiving\nCurrent Students\nFinancial Support\nOverview\nTeaching & Research Appointments\nFellowships\nConference Grants\nExternal Funding\nOther Resources\nProfessional Development\nOverview\nFuture Focus Workshops\n3MT Competition\nCareer Exploration and Development Tools\nTeaching Development and Support\nIndividual Development Plan\nCFP: Whittington Leadership and Innovation Challenge for Ph.D. Students\nEvents\nUpcoming Events\nCalendar\nCommencement\nResources\nAcademic Resources\nHealth and Wellness\nOmbudsperson\nResources for International Graduate Students\nFurther University Resources\nStudent Life\nOverview\nGraduate Student Organizations\nLiving in Pittsburgh\nGraduate Student Parents\nAcademics\nOverview\nAdvising and Mentoring\nAcademic Calendar\nGraduation\nProspective Students\nAdmissions\nOverview\nApplication\nDepartment Admissions Requirements\nInternational Students\nGraduate Certificates\nApplication Fee Waivers\nNon-Degree Application\nRonald E. McNair Scholars Admission Information\nApplication and Requirements\nDepartments and Programs\nInterdisciplinary Experiences\nFinancial Support\nResources for International Graduate Students\nSome 40% of all Dietrich School graduate students are international students from currently over 70 countries. We are a cosmopolitan community of research and learning committed to an environment of inclusion that fosters global understanding and open exchange of intercultural thought. Our international students' diverse and global perspectives enrich all our students' educational experiences, our school, and our university, as well as our city and the nation.\nThe University of Pittsburgh's Office of International Services supports international graduate students with information and advice. Visit the Office of International Services' website to learn about more about their resources and services.\nOther websites international students may find useful include:\nEnglish Language Institute\nProfessional and Academic English Program (PAEP)\nPitt Global\nUnversity Center for International Studies\nOffice of International Services - Immigration Services\nOffice of International Services' Outreach\nHealth Insurance for International Students\nCertification of English Language Fluency for Teaching\nITA English Comprehensibility Testing\nCurrent Students\nFinancial Support\nOverview\nTeaching & Research Appointments\nFellowships\nConference Grants\nExternal Funding\nOther Resources\nProfessional Development\nOverview\nFuture Focus Workshops\n3MT Competition\nCareer Exploration and Development Tools\nTeaching Development and Support\nIndividual Development Plan\nCFP: Whittington Leadership and Innovation Challenge for Ph.D. Students\nEvents\nUpcoming Events\nCalendar\nCommencement\nResources\nAcademic Resources\nHealth and Wellness\nOmbudsperson\nResources for International Graduate Students\nFurther University Resources\nStudent Life\nOverview\nGraduate Student Organizations\nLiving in Pittsburgh\nGraduate Student Parents\nAcademics\nOverview\nAdvising and Mentoring\nAcademic Calendar\nGraduation\nCool Pittsburgh\nIt is no surprise that Pittsburgh has been voted America\u2019s Most Livable City more than once\u2014there truly is something for everyone.\nVisit Pittsburgh \u00bb\nThe Dietrich School of Arts & Sciences Graduate Studies\n910 Cathedral of Learning\n4200 Fifth